00:03:17,419 --> 00:03:23,419
How to Train Your Dragon 2 is a fantasy, action,
adventure film directed by Dean DeBlois.

2
00:06:34,838 --> 00:06:40,838
Five years have passed since Hiccup and Toothless
united the dragons and Vikings of Berk.

3
00:09:52,258 --> 00:09:58,258
Now, they spend their time charting unmapped territories.

4
00:13:09,677 --> 00:13:15,677
During one of their adventures, the pair discover a secret cave that houses
hundreds of wild dragons -- and a mysterious dragon rider.

5
00:16:27,096 --> 00:16:33,096
Now, Hiccup and Toothless find themselves at the center of a
battle to protect Berk from a power-hungry warrior.

6
00:19:44,516 --> 00:19:50,516
Hiccup (voice), played by Jay Baruchel.

7
00:23:01,935 --> 00:23:07,935
Valka (voice), played by Cate Blanchett.

8
00:26:19,354 --> 00:26:25,354
Stoick (voice), played by Gerard Butler.

9
00:29:36,774 --> 00:29:42,774
Gobber (voice), played by Craig Ferguson.

10
00:32:54,193 --> 00:33:00,193
Astrid (voice), played by America Ferrera.

11
00:36:11,612 --> 00:36:17,612
Snotlout (voice), played by Jonah Hill.

12
00:39:29,032 --> 00:39:35,032
How to Train Your Dragon 2 is a 2014 American animated fantasy film written and
directed by Dean DeBlois, based on the book series by Cressida Cowell.

13
00:42:46,451 --> 00:42:52,451
Produced by DreamWorks Animation, it is the second
installment in the How to Train Your Dragon trilogy.

14
00:46:03,870 --> 00:46:09,870
Jay Baruchel, America Ferrera, Gerard Butler, Craig Ferguson, Jonah
Hill, Christopher Mintz-Plasse, Kristen Wiig and T.J.

15
00:49:21,290 --> 00:49:27,290
Miller reprise their roles from the first film, with Cate Blanchett,
Djimon Hounsou, and Kit Harington joining the cast.

16
00:52:38,709 --> 00:52:44,709
Set five years after the events of the first film, it follows 20-year-old Hiccup and his friends as they encounter Valka,
Hiccup's long-lost mother, and Drago Bludvist, a madman who wants to conquer the world by use of a dragon army.

17
00:55:56,129 --> 00:56:02,129
A sequel to How to Train Your Dragon was announced in April
2010, with the outline first drafted in February.

18
00:59:13,548 --> 00:59:19,548
DeBlois, who co-directed the first film, agreed to return on the
condition he would be allowed to make a trilogy.

19
01:02:30,967 --> 01:02:36,967
He cited The Empire Strikes Back (1980) and My Neighbor Totoro (1988) as his main
inspirations, with the expanded scope of the former being particularly influential.

20
01:05:48,387 --> 01:05:54,387
DeBlois and his creative team visited Svalbard to
look for inspirations for the setting.

21
01:09:05,806 --> 01:09:11,806
Composer John Powell returned to score the film.

22
01:12:23,225 --> 01:12:29,225
It was DreamWorks' first film to use scalable multi-core processing
and the studio's new animation and lighting software.

23
01:15:40,645 --> 01:15:46,645
How to Train Your Dragon 2 premiered at the 2014 Cannes Film Festival on May 16, 2014,
and was released in the United States on June 13 by 20th Century Fox.

24
01:18:58,064 --> 01:19:04,064
Like its predecessor, it received critical acclaim, with
praise for its animation and emotional depth.

25
01:22:15,483 --> 01:22:21,483
It grossed $622 million, becoming the 12th-highest-grossing film of 2014.

26
01:25:32,903 --> 01:25:38,903
The film won the Golden Globe for Best Animated Feature and six Annie Awards, including Best
Animated Feature, and was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Animated Feature.

27
01:28:50,322 --> 01:28:56,322
The final installment in the trilogy, How to Train Your
Dragon: The Hidden World, was released in 2019.

28
01:32:07,741 --> 01:32:13,741
A live-action remake is scheduled for release in 2027.

29
01:35:25,161 --> 01:35:31,161
The film explores themes of rescue, husband wife relationship,
sacrifice, parent child relationship, loss of loved one.

30
01:38:42,580 --> 01:38:48,580
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking and intense.
